                "entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                "word": "heteronormative",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "681f3367-f5cd-4a17-947b-4784db46123d",
                        "entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more heteronormative"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8c4766c6-f4af-4f15-93d5-e8dc8fa0cd69",
                        "entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most heteronormative"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                        "entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of or pertaining to the practices and institutions that privilege or value heterosexuality, heterosexual relationships, and traditional gender roles as fundamental and \\\"natural\\\" within society."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "544af3b6-4f65-4fa5-8fc9-08af402d0d22",
                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                "text": "Much of the language used when discussing wedding planning is heteronormative, which can alienate homosexual couples."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72c1dd44-9279-4430-872e-331f05112c93",
                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                "text": "This suggests both that film studies can be heteronormative even when it is analyzing homosexual representations and that close textual analysis is itself structured by heterosexual presumptions and assumptions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "957fad1f-828d-4726-a20a-e6d78fa4f9a7",
                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                "text": "In the same way, homosexuality and bisexuality will always be seen as problematic in heteronormative organizations."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "227fa638-ec75-47d1-88f5-a86c9f7bf015",
                                "sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
                                "text": "Homonationalism needs to be more broadly understood as one dimension of “homonormativity,” which Lisa Duggan described over a decade ago as a gay mindset that does not “contest dominant heteronormative assumptions and institutions but upholds and sustains them.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0a81463b-99b2-44f1-8472-481dee89d8d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "17b239c3-67c3-3bdf-b05e-f6b5179bf142",
                        "source_sense_id": "966c725d-7e6a-39c2-80c8-289b13626ef8",
